{"duration_api_ms":88203,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":0.8602531999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":55871,"cache_read_input_tokens":1151486,"output_tokens":9133,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":619},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":55871,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1148,"cache_read_input_tokens":87934,"cache_creation_input_tokens":307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":307},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1910,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":32,"outputTokens":9133,"cacheReadInputTokens":1151486,"cacheCreationInputTokens":55871,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8600532,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":619,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":55871,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_019D8dHhkwgNtwyHGPU5vpbV","tool_input":{"command":"sed -n 28,200p .theseus/adapter/adapter.yaml | grep -n -B2 -A12 \"x2t\"; ls external/core 2>/dev/null | head -40; wc -l external/core/X2tConverter/src/*.cpp 2>/dev/null; sed -n '/^```yaml/,/^```/p' .theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-docservice.md | head -40; git log --oneline -1"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WQSCMpzatxLmcsqcjMcEmg","tool_input":{"command":"cd /home/claude/euro-office-server.theseus-worktrees/PKT-0036 && sed -n 335,360p external/core/X2tConverter/src/lib/pdf_image.h; ls external/core/DesktopEditor/doctrenderer | head -30; git rev-parse --short HEAD; ls .theseus/oracle .theseus/oracle/perf"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJuwmqcLowcCEN6n3mkHNt","tool_input":{"command":"git -C /home/claude/euro-office-server.theseus-worktrees/PKT-0036 rev-parse --short HEAD"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_014zoEKnoPR7RHo3mr3qM2Ep","tool_input":{"command":"cd /home/claude/euro-office-server.theseus-worktrees/PKT-0036 && echo '{\"packet\":\"PKT-0036\",\"role\":\"diagnostician\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"date\":\"2026-11-02\",\"helped\":{\"ref\":\"oracle/baseline.md\",\"text\":\"The baseline already had raw x2t timings per direction and on large files, so the verdict could be argued from numbers.\"},\"missing\":{\"ref\":\"atlas/x2t.md\",\"text\":\"The card has no metrics or profile of where x2t time goes (V8 init vs layout vs PDF write); the verdict had to be conditional on a profiling packet.\"}}' >> .theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl && grep -q \"^verdict: \" .theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-x2t.md && grep -q \"^goals_hash: dcb03039\" .theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-x2t.md && theseus validate"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":22,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the diagnosis to `.theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-x2t.md`. The verdict is **refactor, staying in C++**, and it is conditional on two first steps: profiling PDF export and building a test oracle. All three acceptance commands pass (`theseus validate`: 0 errors, 1 warning that same-family review is allowed in pilot mode), and the work is committed as `3539077`.\n\n**Why refactor, from the baseline numbers:**\n- **PDF export is where x2t costs users time.** It takes 0.65–1 s even on an empty file, against about 70 ms for ODF output, and 1.3–6.5 s on realistic files.\n- **x2t also drives the save backlog.** Saves are assembled one at a time at about 0.45 s per document, so 200 editors leaving at once wait up to 95 s.\n- **Open is not an x2t problem.** x2t takes only 0.1–0.3 s of an open; the rest is the browser.\n- **The time isn't in x2t's own code.** x2t only routes each conversion. PDF export calls `doct_bin2pdf` (`lib/pdf_image.h:339`), which lays the document out with the editor's JavaScript (sdkjs) running in a V8 engine, then writes the PDF in C++. Changing x2t's language would not touch that.\n- **No language change is allowed yet anyway.** There is no automated test oracle for x2t, so the spec's rule D1 rules out migrate and rewrite.\n\n**Packet plan:**\n- **P1 (wave 0, investigate):** split PDF export and save-conversion time into V8 startup, script load, layout and PDF writing.\n- **P2 (wave 0, characterize):** a corpus oracle run on the installed `x2t` binary, comparing exit codes, output sizes and PDF text and page counts.\n- **P3 (wave 1, refactor):** cut whichever fixed cost P1 shows to be largest.\n\nP1 and P2 declare `requires: [documentserver]`.\n\n**Surprises:**\n- `external/core` is a read-only checkout until a fork exists, so P3 can't land code in this repository. It is told to deliver a patch and a note for humans if the fork still doesn't exist.\n- The fixed ~0.6 s may turn out to be sdkjs code running inside x2t. If P1 shows that, x2t drops to **keep** and the work moves to the sdkjs modules. This is written into \"What would change this verdict\".\n\n**What I couldn't do:**\n- I took no measurements of my own, so how PDF time splits is unknown until P1 runs.\n- Some commands were refused by permissions (reading the server repo's HEAD commit, piped `head`/`wc`/`sed` reads), so I used the card's `base_commit` (the `core` commit), unlike DIAG-docservice which recorded this repository's commit.\n- I filed no spawn requests, because the follow-ups are the plan's own packets.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- The x2t card should record that PDF export runs through `CDoctrenderer` (V8 and sdkjs), so the \"x2t cost\" partly belongs to the sdkjs modules.\n- The card has no metrics or profile yet; P1's results should go there.\n- The card should record that `core` is a read-only checkout, which blocks refactors until a fork exists.\n\nThe packet's Executor log and the friction line in `.theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl` are updated.","ttft_ms":1923,"type":"result","duration_ms":88717,"uuid":"4797a66e-f5d0-4903-aa87-cfd7a09a1df3","ttft_stream_ms":961,"time_to_request_ms":360,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":197,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":27,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":8,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":13,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":29,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":7,"request_build":12},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":61,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":210,"time_to_request_major_faults":59,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":216,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":142,"process_rss_mib_result":243,"process_anon_mib_result":152,"process_peak_rss_mib":254,"process_cpu_ms_turn":3052,"process_wall_ms_turn":88717,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1615,"process_wall_ms_streaming":71071,"main_stream_count":16,"main_stream_event_count":1500,"main_stream_chunk_count":1177,"input_attachments_detail":{